    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0c2e1f7_76000b7d",
        "filename": "pandora/interfaces/pandora_experimental/avrcp.proto",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904823
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-22T02:16:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are not really AVRCP methods, but rather methods related to the media player. Indeed, in this case, the Android device is an AVRCP TG and we\u0027re only trying to do actions on the mediaplayer in order to trigger AVRCP notifications for the CT.\n\nI think we should move these methods in a `mediaplayer.proto` file and keep only AVRCP methods as part of `avrcp.proto`.\n\nTo make it a bit more user friendly, I would also recommend implementing directly one method to go to each state, instead of having a `setPlaybackState` method.\n\nFor instance, `mediaplayer.proto` could look like that:\n\n```\nservice MediaPlayer {\n  rpc Play(PlayRequest) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);\n  rpc Stop(StopRequest) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);\n  rpc Pause(PauseRequest) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);\n  rpc Rewind(RewindRequest) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);\n  rpc FastForward(FastForwardRequest) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);\n  rpc Forward(ForwardRequest) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);\n  rpc Backward(BackwardRequest) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);\n  rpc SetLargeMetadata(google.protobuf.Empty) returns (google.protobuf.Empty);\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "d6eb6c2b34c7cd597207bcdb1978f78a89ee82ac",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
